60 document questions, 6 passages retrieved for each.

  context recall     the golden span was retrieved    40 of 60  (67%)
                     and it was ranked first          25 of 60  (42%)
  context precision  passages from the cited document 12%
  faithfulness       no unsupported claim             38 of 40  (95%)
                     (20 refusals excluded — a refusal makes no claims)

Three of those four numbers were computed without a model. Context recall is a
string comparison against the span the case already carries; context precision
is counting filenames. Both are exact, free and reproducible, and both are
metrics people routinely reach for a judge to estimate.

Only faithfulness needed one, because 'is this claim supported by that
passage' is a reading comprehension question with no string operation behind
it.

Now the part that matters — what recall actually predicts.

  span retrieved     40 cases, 40 answered correctly (100%)
  span not retrieved 20 cases, 0 answered correctly (0%)
                     and 20 of those 20 were refusals

Context recall is not a proxy for correctness here. It is the ceiling on
it. Every case where the passage was not retrieved was a case the system
could not answer, and it said so rather than guessing — which is the
grounding check from §13.11 doing precisely its job.

That is worth knowing before spending a week on prompts. Twenty of these
sixty failures are retrieval failures, and no wording of any instruction
recovers a passage that was never fetched.

Context precision of 12% needs its own care. It counts passages from the
document the case cites, and a passage from another quarter's review is not
useless — for 'which region was strongest', comparing quarters is reasonable
behaviour that this metric calls noise.

2 of the 40 graded answers carried a claim the checker could not
locate. Here is one:
  Southwest was the strongest region in 2024 Q4 at $2,565,933.

Read the flags before believing the score. A faithfulness checker marks
anything absent from the passages it was shown, which includes claims that
are true, in the document, and in a chunk that was not retrieved.

None of this makes the metrics useless. It makes them instruments with known
error, which is the only kind there is. The mistake is quoting faithfulness to
two decimal places without ever reading ten of the flags.
